THE cost of 45 Euros includes the trip, the welcome of the toast with Kaiser beer, made according to the rules of Bavarian genuineness, the disease crate and the German guide – Marco attended a German course in Frankfurt.
And so at night the buses leave for the Brenner.
There's no beer yet.
Suddenly the silence falls in the bus, travelers are asleep.
Better that way, they'll still need their strength.
They stop in Brixen and Holzkirchen, where other buses with Italian license plates on the A9 motorway before Munich take a short break.
When, as expected, Marco's group arrives at 6.30 a.m
Elena, Luca and the others regroup, Marco explains for the last time the attacking program.
First: put on the yellow hat.
"Oktoberfest" on the left there is "Oktoberfest" next to the internet address of Marco's travel agency: "Conoscersiviaggiando.it".
Second: "When they open the doors of the beer marquee it means running!", quotes Marco in the early morning.
"Run!" Running and occupying seats at the bottom of the tent.
"Not in front, otherwise we block, and not all the yellow caps sitting on the same benches, dividing into the adjoining space!"
The mug costs 8.25 Euros, Marco screams.
And don't forget to tip.
"Prove to the security service, that we behave well!
As soon as they leave the seats, they disappear!”
Third: "Tonight at 22.30 on time we meet here again! Got it?"
We're already going for the party.
On the street one attacks as you follow away the yellow caps to the trees, road signs and even to a billboard of a large Bavarian People's Party.
You want to be ready to beat the retreat.
It's the party's second weekend, known as the "Italian weekend."
Exact data does not exist, we are talking about 50 thousand, who leave to cross the Alps and invade marquees, it is claimed that 10% of visitors come specifically from Italy.
The Munich police are strengthened with 7 South Tyrolean agents, Italian volunteers support the Bavarian red criss, which makes a statistic on nationalities, where Italians find themselves in the first place with 200 medical care in front of the British (about 60 medical care) and the Austrians (about 80).
Especially loved by Italians is the marquee of the Hofbräuhaus.
1. Insomnous Nights for Hypo Real Estate creditors
Germany's banking system is relatively stable, Finance Minister Peer Steinbrück confirmed last week.
It is good that the politician used the word "relative" and also hinted, that the German banking sector was not spared from critical developments.
Because the crisis began at the weekend.
Real estate lender Hypo Real Estate, noted in the DAX, obtains from a consortium of German banks a billionaire credit, in order to protect itself from turmoil in the markets.
A person experienced in the situation told Reuters on Monday, support credits would reach up to 35 billion Euros.
Hypo Real Estate only has to pay interest for the required party.
Money comes from both private banks and the public.
At the bottom are the losses of the Depfa affiliate.
According to a newspaper, the state lender has refinanced itself in a very short term – which is no longer possible due to distrust in the markets.
In the first half of 2008 the bank's reserves had shrunk by 95% to 2.37 million Euros, even the share of own capital yielded from 1.6 to 1.45.
Current incomes and net annuities from financial affairs had fallen to 0 compared to last year, earnings from increments of both applications and certain shares as well as the liquidation of provisions in credits fell more than 70% to 5 million Euros.
Only thanks to higher incomes from the repayment of subordinate compensation costs that come both from the restructuring of the former Depfa group and from the repayment of interest according to the single text of tax laws and the management of business for entrepreneurial consortia, the negative profit was quite moderate with about 16%.
The former public lender after being privatised in 1990 had been lost in speculation on commercial retail loans, which were spuffered into the Aareal Bank.
Given that the income in classic state funding was too low, Depfa engaged more in infrastructure projects and the financing of joint projects of private and state investors (PPPs) and diversified internationally.
Hypo Real Estate now has to amortize the value of the affiliate, which will have a fundamental material effect on the group's profit and loss account.
The fact is that the dividends have been erased.
Already in 2007 they had been reduced by 2/3.
Hypo Real Estate after Depfa's uptaking is an important financier of the state and infrastructure.
It is more dependent on refinancing on the market among banks in comparison with other institutions, because it does not have customer fiduciary deposits.
Due to the collapse of the American investment bank Lehman Brothers two weeks ago the granting of credits among banks has largely dried up, because banks hoard liquidity.
Hypo Real Estate annually requires a part of Depfa’s credit portfolio – about 50 billion – in the short term the means of refinancing.
According to Hypo Real Estate's notice, the group's financial needs have been covered by credit for a time and the enterprise protected by the influence of the mostly non-functioning international monetary markets.
From other sources you feel, that thanks to the money the refinancing is secured until the end of 2009.
HRE Steering Committee Chairman Georg Funke on the contrary said that the HRE Group will not need monetary markets in a short time.
The Bundesbank and the National Financial Supervisory Service Authority (BaFin) are based on the fact that the HRE Group's marketability is still assured.
This is hoped for the bank's equities and creditors.
With a view to the dynamics and imponderability of the crisis there will be no guarantee.
Funding may not be used completely.
But even the opposite is not to be ruled out.
After Sunday night the bank, according to reports, it was about to fail, the momentary bailout failed to calm the spirits.
The share runs down 75% to 3.30 Euros.
Mortgage courses hold up pretty well.
While front-grade debts are almost immovable, they give off posterged credit courses.
The mortgages of the Württemberg-Hypo affiliate are mainly affected, understandably, the starting points expiring beyond 2009.
Before Della HRE mortgages seemed a speculative alternative investment, now their value must, after the strengthening of the crisis of the banks and of the institution itself, which with the Depfa's relief has escalated the crisis, will have to be considered dependent on the stability of the international financial system.
As long as central banks, governments and less damaged banks are still ready, you can count on depreciation of annualities within the deadline.
Or it comes into operation, what no one dares to hope – for the financial crisis to be overcome within the next 15 months.
But with regard to information overturned due to partial statization, the almost certain probability has become a justified hope.
It will mainly create long-term investors some sleepless nights with the decision whether to split from their commitments.
Short-term investors may bring to an end the carry-over of losses for future payments of the compensatory capital gains tax.
Sylvana and Bento-Box secrets
When Sylvana Hiltrop, 16-year-old, on the first day of school should show up at Tachibana Highschool, the girls start giggling: The German is completely "kawaii"!
What does that mean?
Sylvana already knows the word from Mangas-in the new Exchange Log tells of Japan.
The first day of school in Japan
How excited I was.
I even had fifa to go to school.
I drive on the edge of Tokio towards Kawasaki and I need 40 minutes by train to get to Tachibana Highschool.
I had to find the road myself and luckily I didn't miss.
The beginning of the first hour of class does not seem to have been set as well as by us in Lower Saxony.
The schoolchildren arrive slowly from 8 a.m. onwards, until 8.40 a.m. begins a brief interview with the professor, the so-called "home room".
But before it was up to me to the lesson to introduce myself.
Meanwhile, I'm not the guy who speaks willingly in front of people, plus in front of a class of 40 schoolchildren
Since I didn't have a school uniform yet, I put on an old skirt of my host mother, along with a shirt, blue socks and black leather shoes.
Dressed like this, I posed in front of the chair and tried to pronounce well: "Sayonara Wo she Sylvana..."- my name is Sylvana, I'm from Germany and I'll celebrate my birthday in a week.
At that time I was very happy that I had already started learning the language two years ago.
The 31 girls in the class whispered, chuckled and made a sign and I constantly heard the word "Kawaii."
I already knew this from my Mangas.
It belongs to the essential lexicon of Japanese girls to survive and means "cute, sweet".
Then I ran quickly to my place.
The girl next to me grinned, for her it was an honor to sit next to an exchange student
The rest of the class hour had continued quietly, but when she played the gong, I was assailed in the true sense of the word.
Everything they spoke disorderly and giggled and annoyed me with questions – then it’s really difficult to understand Japanese English.
In the break everyone opened their Bento.
My host mother also gave me the basket for the Lunch - it's different from the boring German sandwiches.
I had risotto with spices, sausages, cucumber salad and algae, fruit and a kind of rolls with meat and tofu ..
I don't even know exactly what I eat in Japan.
Things look strange and taste entirely new.
Done is, that everything is really good.
Perhaps except the plums put in salt, brrr!
Bentos aren’t just lunch at Japanese schools.
It happens sometimes that a girl gives a Bento made by herself, prepared quite artistically, with the hope then to get acquainted with the boy during recreation.
I've read it in my Manga comics.
I'm really curious, if I can find out.
"Why just Japan? "I was asked by my friends when I told, that I wanted to go for a year to school in Japan.
I've always said:
"Because it fascinates me "
Finally, I have been reading the Mangas with fervor for years.
And to better understand the comics and the culture they contain, sooner or later I began to learn the Japanese language a bit.
I was completely convinced to come there once.
I’m also fascinated by tradition, customs.
They're keeping a lot here.
On the one hand, Japan is a place of technology and the latest tendencies on the opposite side: severe, disciplined and traditional.
Given that everything is organized well, I have never felt lost, even though Tokyo is the largest city I have never seen in my life.”
1. Even rats have feelings
A rat or cockroach flees when they feel danger. Does that mean, that they also feel fear?
Neurologist scientist Joseph Le Doux is convinced of this: even many animals have feelings.
4. But how could it occur if, when they behave in the same way, they have the same sensations as us?
In the Internet "Edge" for some years are published articles by well-known scientists.
6. SPIEGEL ONLINE in a series presents chosen answers to the question: "What do you think is true, without being able to prove it?"
I believe that animals have feelings or other states of conscience, without me or someone so far being able to prove it, since we cannot even prove that other men have consciousness.
But in this case we at least have to hope, that all human brains have the same basic configuration.
9. As soon as we turn to the other species and ask questions about feeling or in general about consciousness, we enter into an impracticable territory, so that the reference base does not match.
When a rat finds himself in a dangerous situation, he does the same things that the other animals do too. That is, he pretends to be dead, flees or attacks.
People behave in a similar way, from where some scientists understand that there is a comparable subjective feeling.
I don't believe that.
Two aspects of brain structure make it difficult for us to convey our feeling towards animals.
On the one hand it often connects the lateral prefrontal cortex with human awareness, the associated circuits (this for its direct participation in short memory and executive and control functions).
In man this large area is much more developed than in other primates and it seems that among other creatures it lacks completely.
At least in those aspects of our awareness dependent on the prefrontal cortex, including knowledge, who we are, and the ability to plan and to decide, we thus admit the foundation on the assumption that man differs even from other primates.
Another dramatic peculiarity should present itself in man's way of speaking: since a large part of life is connected to the language, it is often said to be related to consciousness.
In this case animals could be excluded.
Although awareness does not depend on the language, it would influence it so that the awareness of the animal, as it is done, certainly differs greatly from the circumstances of our consciousness.
That’s why it’s hard to find out how consciousness can be seen in other animals.
If it is not possible to measure it as an internal and subjective thing, in analyzing it through one's own experience due to the special hardware, their research will pose great problems.
Most interpretations refer to the content of conscious experience, but apart from that there is another aspect of consciousness to which for science it would be easier to access.
We could analyze the processes of animal consciousness without regard to their contents, and precisely this happens in studies on the short memory of primates, in particular the example of visualization.
So for this principle that Christof Koch und Francis Crick follows, we move first to the neural correlates of consciousness than to the causal mechanisms: both could be identical but not necessarily.
In an interesting way, this principle also highlights the value of the prefrontal cortex for the implementation of visualization.
So, what is outlined for feelings?
I impute them to the fact that an emotional system like that of fear is activated in one of its conscious activities of the brain.
What we indicate as "fear" is therefore the mental state in which we find ourselves when the activity of the defense system located in the brain (or its consequences, such as the reactions of the body) occupies working memory.
Seen in this way the feelings are closely connected to the regions of the cortex, which characterize primates and in particular the human being.
With talking nature, subtle nuances of feeling are created, because with the help of words and grammar we can distinguish and categorize situations, to describe them to others.
Compared to this Antonio Damasio, for example, believes that the feelings result from more primitive activities of the regions of the body of the sensations of the cortex and paleocephalus, similar to Jack Pankseep, who, however, focused more on the paleocephale.
Since this network hasn't changed much in the course of human evolution, this could absolutely be part of the species-extensive feelings.
On a purely theoretical level I cannot contradict it, but I consider it unprovable.
Pankseep argues that what for rats and humans appears to be afraid, is probably felt with the senses in both cases: but in what way could it occur, if rats and human beings feel the same thing when they behave in a similar way?
A cockroach in case of danger flees as if he also felt the fear?
In my eyes the mere similarity of behavior cannot yet prove any vital resemblance.
Neural comparison continues to help: rats and humans have similar paleoencephales, cockroaches not even a brain.
Is paleoencephalus responsible for feelings?
And even if you could prove it for human beings : how is it that you would like to prove it on rats?
I think rats and other mammals, maybe even insects (who knows?), have feelings.
I didn’t know how to prove it.
And since their feelings are fundamentally different from ours (since human consciousness is based on specific circuits and language), I prefer to study emotional behavior rather than the emotional sensations of rats.
In any case, there are neural progress here, as long as it renounces the same procedure on rats and men.
As I don’t research language and consciousness in rats, so I don’t do it on their emotions, I don’t even know if they exist.
This can be considered short-sighted, but I prefer to take steps forward, rather than slam a wall all the time.
I'm an emotional practice.
The President of UEFA Platini: postponement for Poland and Ukraine
Deputy Premier Iwan Wasjunik said preparations will soon be placed under the direct responsibility of the president and prime minister.
