It also includes college sweatshirts, retro boxers, cashmere cardigans, cotton pants, marinara T-shirts, baby-dolls, mini short...
Intimate clothing designed to be comfortable.
And it's a shame to use them as underwear.
They're too beautiful.
"I want to be a young mom, the candidate doesn't bother me"
The great resemblance to her sister didn’t prevent her from developing her own personality.
Monica Cruz is small, but full of vitality.
Currently, the Cruz sisters have taken their new business very seriously in the field of fashion.
For Monica, they're much more than beautiful girls and celebrities who lend their names.
It was in Paris for the promotion that the Mango signature made of its new headquarters, in addition to the presentation of the most important awards that the Spanish fashion house sponsors.
Warm and shy, he conquers you quickly.
Tell us what you do in Paris.
I came to present the new collection that we designed my sister Penelope and me for the autumn-winter season of Mango, as well as to participate in the presentation of the second edition of the 'Mango Fashion Awards' and dinner at the Opera in honor of Valentino.
Let's say, a very busy day, but at the same time, exciting.
From what elements does your new collection for Mango start in this fourth working season for the Spanish home?
Both my sister and I like the cinema of the 50's and 60's, from here we get various inspirations.
Then, I love getting lost in the city and observing how women dress, how they combine and mix their own clothes. I do it frequently.
Dancer, actress and stylist, you're a very versatile woman, aren't you?
I think so, even if in the end, everything converges and there are many elements in common.
Since I was a child, I liked clothes; I wanted to go to my grandmother’s house to rummage through my aunt’s closets and see her clothes.
It was a bomb better even than going to the playground.
Then, once a dancer, I've always paid a lot of attention to dressing.
You know that dancers really like to have their own style to go to class and essays, to look in the mirror and feel good.
And in the role of actress, when they give you the wardrobe is the moment when you really meet the character.
So, everything goes together, yes, with a lot of respect for stylists and professionalism.
Not long ago, you turned 30, did you get into crisis?
But no.
Never felt better, I like the idea of 30 years.
I find that at that age women are mature and have a good experience to savor life by making fewer mistakes.
The biological clock doesn't scare me.
I've done the things that I wanted since I was little and that gave me a lot of inner happiness.
So you think you're a mother or not?
Of course, I know that I will be a mother because my own body asks me and also I want to be a young mother, I don’t want to miss this.
As for the candidate, I don't worry too much.
What I'm going to do is give a lot of happiness to my son and educate him with a lot
As for the cinema, you're waiting for a few films shot last year.
That's right, and I really want them out.
Being a woman who comes from the theater, I'm very impatient and restless, I'd like everything immediately and clearly, but it can't always be like that.
I want "La última hora" and "En busca de la tumba de Cristo" out.
Let's see if you'll like them
A few days ago, you debuted on the catwalk with Naomi Campbell, right?
Well, don't say that.
It wasn't that I was on the catwalk as a model.
Simply Naomi Campbell, whom I've known for a long time, called me to invite me to go to London to take part in a charity show for her "Women for a Better World" organization and the clothes we've exhibited - I've brought two pieces from our collection for Mango - they've been auctioned to raise money for this Naomi NGO.
People don't know this tender side of Naomi.
So many things are said about her, that I who have known her for a long date can confirm to you that they are not so true.
Also, I'm with this good part where you're involved.
He asked me to parade for a noble cause, but if he had asked me to do the pine, I'd have done it anyway.
If it's to help the women of the third world, you can't back down.
Recidivist drivers of alcoholism will have to install "alcohock"
The Ministry of the Interior requires that drivers with three administrative penalties for excessive blood alcohol, install in his car the system that prevents the driving of the vehicle while intoxicated or if you do not blow into the appropriate device.
The measure was announced last June and is already included in the annual report of the State Attorney General, according to which it will be a one-year pilot project.
The purpose of this project is the reintegration of the driver, since this will have to attend a road rehabilitation course.
This initiative, in addition to the Attorney General for Road Safety, will be attended by the General Directorate of Traffic (DGT) and the Fondazione Istituto Tecnologico per la Sicurezza dell'Automobile (FITSA).
According to statistics, between 30% and 75% of motorists reported more than once for drunk driving then return to driving the car.
Alcoholic would avoid it, because it is a system connected to the vehicle that measures the rate of alcohol in exhaled air and prevents you from setting the car in motion if the driver does not blow, or when a higher concentration of alcohol is detected than that allowed.
The cost is more than 1000 euros and would be borne by the sanctioned.
In this regard, a study conducted in the United States in 2007 has shown that vehicles equipped with such devices make it possible to reduce up to 65% of infractions committed during the first year of introduction.
And in Spain it's estimated it could save the lives of 115 people a year.
The measure is limited to administrative penalties for two reasons: curb these behaviors before they become criminal offences.
And to facilitate its development, since legal reform can be carried out on an ordinary basis, and, without a doubt, the reform necessary for criminal procedure would require an organic law.
However, the device is not yet available on the Spanish market in any commercial solution, although it has already been introduced experimentally in some industrial and public vehicles.
Just tomorrow, the Congress of Deputies will vote on a PSOE initiative proposing to install this system in school buses, as has already been done in France.
In Mexico, and without "peep-toes"
